## 3. Bug found (exact diff vs. canonical)

The repo file differed from the canonical implementation in three ways:
* condition was `weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11` instead of `month === 11 && weekOfYear < 5` (misses all end-of-year weeks that are numbered 52/53 but still belong to the next year);
* the whole `month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52` branch (return `year - 1`) was missing;
* used a cached `const year` / `return year` instead of `this.year()`.

Note: the task's expected values are ISO-like week-years, which in dayjs correspond to locales with `yearStart: 4` (all of them also have `weekStart: 1`: en-gb, en-in, en-tt, fr, cs, sk, zh, zh-cn). With the default `en` locale (weekStart 0 / doy 6) the correct values are the moment-`en` ones, which the existing test asserts; the canonical implementation satisfies both.

